//! tr kodlu 3 dil=en
// 06 — Input: reading data from the user.
// What it teaches: reading a line with input("question"), turning the text into a number with int(),
// falling back to a default when the input is empty.
// Builds on: types and conversions (03), text (04), conditions (05).
// Run (from the project root): tr examples/en/06_input.tr
//   Run it interactively and answer the questions; if you just press Enter the default value is used.
//   Where no input arrives (standard input empty or closed) the program goes on with the defaults.
//   In the debugger (F5) input() does not work: the session has no standard input; use Ctrl+F5 or run it in a terminal.

// input(question) writes the question and gives the line the user typed as a String.
// If nothing is typed an empty string ("") comes back.
TR_kw_var person = TR_fn_input("What is your name? ")
TR_kw_if person == "" {
    person = "Guest"
}
TR_fn_print("Hello, {person}!")

// input always gives a String; when a number is needed it is converted with int() or float().
TR_kw_var age_text = TR_fn_input("How old are you? ")
TR_kw_var age = 20
TR_kw_if age_text != "" {
    age = TR_fn_int(age_text)
}
TR_fn_print("Next year you will be {age + 1}.")

// --- Try it yourself ---
// 1. Ask for two numbers and print their sum.
// 2. Type "abc" as the age: int() fails. You will learn to handle that error in example 13.
